  "section": "CRS-10",
  "name": "attachment-encrypt",
  "description": "Attachment encryption: keys = aes_key (bytes 0-31) || mac_key (bytes 32-63); padded = plaintext || zero bytes up to padded_size; blob = iv || AES-256-CBC-PKCS7(aes_key, iv, padded) || HMAC-SHA256(mac_key, iv || ciphertext); digest = SHA-256(blob). The AES-256-CBC encryption, the HMAC-SHA256 and the SHA-256 digest of every case were run by the oracle process (its standard-primitive operations) on Comma-chosen keys, IVs and plaintexts; each MAC also equals the oracle incremental-MAC operation used as a single-chunk HMAC-SHA256, and each ciphertext decrypts back through the oracle. padded_size and the byte layout of the blob follow the CRS-10 rules [source] (see padded-size.json). Decryption test: verify mac, verify digest, decrypt, keep the first plaintext_size bytes.",
